{# ═══════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════
   THREE SEPARATE READS — the Grey Deer settled Risk Envelope band (macro.html)

   Consumes `risk_envelope` (site/riskdata/risk_envelope.json, composed by
   engine/risk_envelope.py). Renders NOTHING when the artifact is absent — an
   honest missing section beats an invented one.

   ── The design job ────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
   The page above this band already answers "what regime am I in". It answers it
   with ONE number, and until now it narrated the disagreement away in a prose
   aside ("a rotation read, not a high-beta cue"). This band answers a different
   question — "do the market reads agree?" — and it is built so the answer cannot be
   averaged: co-equal rows, each carrying its own state, its own plain clause, and
   its OWN clock. Three answers are shown; exactly two of them are compared.

   ── GD-2R1 (Sol post-merge review) ────────────────────────────────────────────
   Two corrections landed here:
   · The spine now spans the TWO MARKET READS only. Capital policy moved out of it
     into its own inset strip with no rail, because a posture derived from zero
     policies cannot agree or disagree with a market reading — carrying a rail would
     have said it does. Different structure = different kind of statement.
   · All behavioural copy is gone while zero policies exist. There is no stance chip
     and no action instruction anywhere in this band; the capital strip reports the
     literal state "no Grey Deer policy active" and advises nothing. Guidance returns
     only when a registered policy exists to carry it.

   ── The signature: the split spine ────────────────────────────────────────────
   Under the reserved-hue law (MASTER_PRODUCT_DESIGN_SYSTEM_V1 §1) hue may mean
   exactly five things — market direction, health/severity, wayfinding, epistemic
   tier, or lock. "Agreement" is none of them, so coherence may NOT be a colour.
   It is encoded structurally instead: the two MARKET-READ rows share one continuous
   rail when they agree, and the rail BREAKS into separate marks when they do
   not. One line = one truth; separate marks = separate truths. No legend needed, and
   it survives both themes and the zh 红涨绿跌 flip because it derives from the
   same tokens that flip.

   Each row's ink then falls straight out of the same law:
     · trend   → direction ink (--ink-up/--ink-down), the market's direction
     · hazard  → health ink (--ink-ok/--ink-warn/--ink-act), severity
     · policy  → achromatic AND rail-less, because zero policies means nothing is
                 restricted, there is no meaning for hue to carry, and it is not a
                 party to the agreement the rail encodes
   In the contradictory case the two market rows are therefore literally different
   hues by construction — the disagreement is visible before a word is read.

   ── Deliberate omissions ──────────────────────────────────────────────────────
   · NO 01/02/03 markers. Numbering asserts a sequence; these three questions are
     orthogonal by design, which IS the thesis. Numbering them would be a lie.
   · NO motion. Motion law: an animated element must encode a live/ongoing fact,
     and settled data does not pulse. The stillness is the point — it is what
     will distinguish this from the GD-3 live lane.
   · NO falsifier/refutation vocabulary anywhere (operator ruling 2026-07-27).
     Technicals, receipts and state enums live in the drawer, never at rest.
   ═══════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════ #}

{% set _re = risk_envelope %}
{% if _re and _re.get('schema') == 'mastermind.risk_envelope/v1' %}
{% set _ms = _re.get('measured_state') or {} %}
{% set _hz = _re.get('hazard_summary') or {} %}
{% set _co = _re.get('coherence') or {} %}
{% set _ps = _re.get('policy_summary') or {} %}
{% set _prov = (_re.get('provenance') or {}).get('sources') or [] %}
{% set _stage = _hz.get('stage') %}
{% set _coh = _co.get('state') %}
{% set _split = _coh in ('MIXED', 'CONTRADICTORY') %}

{# ── the leading hazard source: whose read set the stage. Used for the clause so
     the row names the actual organ instead of speaking in the abstract. ── #}
{% set _ns = namespace(lead=none, ms=none) %}
{% for s in _prov %}
  {% if s.role == 'hazard_evidence' and s.hazard_stage == _stage and _ns.lead is none %}
    {% set _ns.lead = s %}
  {% endif %}
  {% if s.role == 'measured_state' and _ns.ms is none %}
    {% set _ns.ms = s %}
  {% endif %}
{% endfor %}
{# The trend organ already publishes its own bilingual STATE label — reuse it verbatim
   so this band and the hero above never drift into two names for one state. #}
{% set _fresh = (_re.get('freshness') or {}).get('per_source') or {} %}
{# source_id → human name, so even the drawer names organs rather than slugs #}
{% set _names_en = {} %}
{% set _names_zh = {} %}
{% for s in _prov %}
  {% if _names_en.update({s.source_id: (s.label_en or s.source_id)}) %}{% endif %}
  {% if _names_zh.update({s.source_id: (s.label_zh or s.label_en or s.source_id)}) %}{% endif %}
{% endfor %}
{% set _ms_detail = (_ns.ms.detail if _ns.ms else {}) or {} %}
{% set _ms_label_en = _ms_detail.get('state_label_en') or 'Risk-on' %}
{% set _ms_label_zh = _ms_detail.get('state_label_zh') or '风险偏好' %}

{# ── direction ink for the trend row ── #}
{% set _ms_ink = {'RISK_ON': 'var(--ink-up)', 'RISK_OFF': 'var(--ink-down)',
                  'MIXED': 'var(--ink-2)'}.get(_ms.get('verdict'), 'var(--prov-ink)') %}
{# ── health ink for the hazard row; null takes the epistemic tone, never a health one ── #}
{% set _hz_ink = {'NONE': 'var(--ink-ok)', 'FRAGILE': 'var(--ink-warn)',
                  'TRANSMITTING': 'var(--ink-act)', 'BREAKDOWN': 'var(--ink-act)'}
                 .get(_stage, 'var(--prov-ink)') %}

{# ── plain-word answers. Internal enums never reach the glance tier. ── #}
{% set _hz_word_en = {'NONE': 'Nothing breaking', 'FRAGILE': "Something's fragile",
                      'TRANSMITTING': 'Damage is spreading', 'BREAKDOWN': 'Broken'}
                     .get(_stage, 'Not enough to say') %}
{% set _hz_word_zh = {'NONE': '未见断裂', 'FRAGILE': '出现脆弱',
                      'TRANSMITTING': '损伤扩散', 'BREAKDOWN': '已断裂'}
                     .get(_stage, '证据不足') %}

<div class="panel span12 gde-band" id="risk-envelope-band">

  <div class="gde-head">
    <div>
      <span class="gde-eyebrow"><span class="l-en">Three reads, kept separate</span><span class="l-zh">三项判读，各自独立</span></span>
      {# "market reads", not "the reads": capital policy sits below and is deliberately
         NOT part of this comparison (GD-2R1 §0.5). The zh title said 三项 ("all three")
         and was simply wrong once policy left the spine. #}
      <h2 class="gde-h2"><span class="l-en">Do the market reads agree?</span><span class="l-zh">市场判读一致吗？</span></h2>
    </div>
    <span class="gde-stamp tnum"
          data-tip-en="Settled session — the close these reads were taken from. Each source below also keeps its own clock."
          data-tip-zh="已结算交易日 — 本次判读所依据的收盘。下方每个来源另有各自的时间戳。">
      <span class="l-en">Settled</span><span class="l-zh">已结算</span> {{ _re.get('source_session') or '—' }}
    </span>
  </div>

  {# ══ THE ANSWER — this section's primary question, answered first ══ #}
  {# EN and ZH each keep their bold clause INSIDE one span: separate elements would
     collapse to an inter-element space, which reads as a stray gap in CJK. #}
  <p class="gde-lead">
    {% if _coh == 'CONTRADICTORY' %}
      <span class="l-en"><b>No — they disagree.</b> The trend read and the damage read point opposite ways. Both are shown, unchanged.</span>
      <span class="l-zh"><b>不一致。</b>趋势判读与损伤判读方向相反。两者原样并列，未做平均。</span>
    {% elif _coh == 'MIXED' %}
      <span class="l-en"><b>Not fully.</b> One read can't be made cleanly today. What we can see is shown below, unchanged.</span>
      <span class="l-zh"><b>并不完全一致。</b>今日有一项无法干净判读，可见部分原样列于下方，未做平均。</span>
    {% else %}
      {# "both", not "all three": capital policy is not one of the compared reads. #}
      <span class="l-en"><b>Yes — both market reads point the same way.</b> Neither is contradicting the other today.</span>
      <span class="l-zh"><b>一致——两项市场判读方向相同。</b>今日两者之间没有矛盾。</span>
    {% endif %}
  </p>

  {# ══ THE THREE READS — co-equal by construction, never ranked, never merged ══ #}
  <div class="gde-reads{% if _split %} is-split{% endif %}">

    {# ── 1 · measured trend ─────────────────────────────────────────────────── #}
    <div class="gde-read" style="--gde-c: {{ _ms_ink }}">
     <div class="gde-row">
      <span class="gde-q"><span class="l-en">Is the trend still there?</span><span class="l-zh">趋势还在吗？</span></span>
      <p class="gde-a">
        {% if _ms.get('usable') and _ms.get('verdict') %}
          <span class="l-en">{{ _ms_label_en }}</span><span class="l-zh">{{ _ms_label_zh }}</span
          >{# Direction NEVER travels by hue alone. Under zh 红涨绿跌 this row's
             direction ink turns red — the same red the hazard row uses for danger —
             so without a sign a zh reader sees two identical reds and loses the
             disagreement. The arrow is what keeps "up" readable as up. #}<span
            class="gde-arr" aria-hidden="true">{{ {'RISK_ON': '▲', 'RISK_OFF': '▼'}.get(_ms.get('verdict'), '▶') }}</span>
        {% else %}
          <span class="l-en">Can't read it today</span><span class="l-zh">今日无法判读</span>
        {% endif %}
      </p>
      <p class="gde-c">
        {% if _ms.get('usable') and _ms.get('score') is not none %}
          <span class="l-en">Slow trend read, carried unchanged from the score above —
            <a class="gde-quote tnum" href="#regime-radar">{{ _ms.get('score') }}<span class="gde-outof">/100</span></a>.</span>
          <span class="l-zh">慢速趋势判读，原样取自上方评分 —
            <a class="gde-quote tnum" href="#regime-radar">{{ _ms.get('score') }}<span class="gde-outof">/100</span></a>。</span>
        {% else %}
          <span class="l-en">The trend source didn't settle for this session, so we're not quoting a stale one.</span>
          <span class="l-zh">趋势来源本交易日未结算，因此不引用过期读数。</span>
        {% endif %}
      </p>
      {# a coverage problem is a caveat that changes how the answer reads, so it sits
         beside the clock rather than only in the drawer (doctrine §9.8) #}
      {% set _msf = _fresh.get(_ns.ms.source_id) if _ns.ms else none %}
      <span class="gde-clock tnum">{{ _ms.get('as_of') or '—' }}{% if _msf and _msf.state != 'FRESH' %}
        <span class="gde-flag">{% if _msf.state == 'STALE' %}<span class="l-en">· older than this session</span><span class="l-zh">· 早于本交易日</span>{% else %}<span class="l-en">· didn't publish</span><span class="l-zh">· 未发布</span>{% endif %}</span>{% endif %}</span>
     </div>
    </div>

    {# ── 2 · transition hazard + the evidence drawer ─────────────────────────── #}
    <div class="gde-read" style="--gde-c: {{ _hz_ink }}">
     <div class="gde-row">
      <span class="gde-q"><span class="l-en">Is anything breaking?</span><span class="l-zh">有什么正在断裂？</span></span>
      <p class="gde-a">
        <span class="l-en">{{ _hz_word_en }}</span><span class="l-zh">{{ _hz_word_zh }}</span>
      </p>
      <p class="gde-c">
        {% if _stage is none %}
          <span class="l-en">A source we need didn't settle today, so we're not calling this either way.</span>
          <span class="l-zh">今日缺少必需来源的结算数据，因此不作任何判定。</span>
        {% elif _stage == 'NONE' %}
          <span class="l-en">We looked at every source we need and none of them shows damage.</span>
          <span class="l-zh">已核对全部必需来源，均未见损伤。</span>
        {% else %}
          {# The onset date is the SOURCE's own retrospective reading, not this read's
             lifecycle clock (hazard_summary.stage_since is null in V0), so the sentence
             attributes it to the source rather than claiming it as ours. #}
          {% set _onset = (_ns.lead.detail.get('state_since') if _ns.lead and _ns.lead.detail else none) %}
          <span class="l-en">{{ (_ns.lead.label_en if _ns.lead else 'A tracked group') }} is damaged while the index holds{% if _onset %} — its own read has said so since {{ _onset }}{% endif %}.</span>
          <span class="l-zh">{{ (_ns.lead.label_zh if _ns.lead else '受追踪的一组标的') }}受损，而指数仍在支撑{% if _onset %}——该来源自 {{ _onset }} 起即如此判读{% endif %}。</span>
        {% endif %}
      </p>
      {# the clock column means "when was this read taken", not "when did the state
         begin" — the since-date already sits in the clause above, and conflating the
         two is how a months-old state starts looking like a stale source #}
      {% set _unread = _hz.get('unreadable_sources') or [] %}
      <span class="gde-clock tnum">{{ (_ns.lead.as_of if _ns.lead else none) or _re.get('source_session') or '—' }}{% if _unread %}
        <span class="gde-flag"><span class="l-en">· {{ _unread | length }} source{{ 's' if _unread | length != 1 else '' }} couldn't be read</span><span class="l-zh">· {{ _unread | length }} 个来源无法读取</span></span>{% endif %}</span>
     </div>

      {# Tier 2/3 lives here: source states, per-source clocks, contradictions,
         and the machine receipt. The summary says what is inside AND why to open. #}
      <details class="gde-disc">
        <summary>
          <span class="l-en">Evidence — {{ _prov | length }} sources{% if _co.get('contradiction_count') %}, {{ _co.get('contradiction_count') }} disagreement{{ 's' if _co.get('contradiction_count') != 1 else '' }}{% endif %}</span>
          <span class="l-zh">证据 — {{ _prov | length }} 个来源{% if _co.get('contradiction_count') %}，{{ _co.get('contradiction_count') }} 处分歧{% endif %}</span>
        </summary>
        <div class="gde-disc-body">
          <div class="gde-tblwrap">
            <table class="gde-tbl">
              <thead><tr>
                <th><span class="l-en">Source</span><span class="l-zh">来源</span></th>
                <th><span class="l-en">Its own read</span><span class="l-zh">自身读数</span></th>
                <th><span class="l-en">As of</span><span class="l-zh">数据日期</span></th>
                <th><span class="l-en">Freshness</span><span class="l-zh">新鲜度</span></th>
              </tr></thead>
              <tbody>
              {% for s in _prov %}
                <tr>
                  <td class="l">{% if s.label_en %}<span class="l-en">{{ s.label_en }}</span><span class="l-zh">{{ s.label_zh or s.label_en }}</span>{% else %}<span class="tnum">{{ s.source_id }}</span>{% endif %}</td>
                  <td class="tnum">{{ s.state if s.state is not none else '—' }}{% if s.score is not none %} · {{ s.score }}{% endif %}</td>
                  <td class="tnum">{{ s.as_of or '—' }}</td>
                  <td>
                    {% if s.coverage == 'FRESH' %}<span class="l-en">This session</span><span class="l-zh">本交易日</span>
                    {% elif s.coverage == 'STALE' %}<span class="gde-warn"><span class="l-en">Older than this session</span><span class="l-zh">早于本交易日</span></span>
                    {% else %}<span class="gde-warn"><span class="l-en">Did not publish</span><span class="l-zh">未发布</span></span>{% endif %}
                    {%- if s.required %} <span class="gde-req"><span class="l-en">required</span><span class="l-zh">必需</span></span>{% endif %}
                  </td>
                </tr>
              {% endfor %}
              </tbody>
            </table>
          </div>

          {% if _co.get('contradictions') %}
          <p class="gde-disc-h"><span class="l-en">Where they disagree</span><span class="l-zh">分歧所在</span></p>
          <ul class="gde-conflicts">
            {% for c in _co.get('contradictions') %}
            <li>
              <span class="l-en">{{ _names_en.get(c.left, c.left) }} reads <b>{{ c.left_state }}</b> while {{ _names_en.get(c.right, c.right) }} reads <b>{{ c.right_state }}</b>.</span>
              <span class="l-zh">{{ _names_zh.get(c.left, c.left) }} 读为 <b>{{ c.left_state }}</b>，而 {{ _names_zh.get(c.right, c.right) }} 读为 <b>{{ c.right_state }}</b>。</span>
            </li>
            {% endfor %}
          </ul>
          {% endif %}

          <p class="gde-receipt tnum">
            {{ _re.get('definition_id') }} · bundle {{ _re.get('bundle_id') }} ·
            coverage {{ _re.get('data_state') }} ·
            coherence {{ _coh }} (scope {{ _co.get('scope') }}) ·
            stage {{ _stage if _stage is not none else 'null' }} ({{ _hz.get('stage_reason') }}) ·
            stage_since null ({{ _hz.get('stage_since_basis') }})
            {%- if _hz.get('capped_sources') %} · capped at source competence: {{ _hz.get('capped_sources') | join(', ') }}{% endif %} ·
            engine/risk_envelope.py
          </p>
        </div>
      </details>
    </div>

  </div>{# /.gde-reads — the spine covers the MARKET READS and stops here #}

  {# ── Capital policy — ORTHOGONAL, deliberately outside the spine ────────────
     GD-2R1 §0.5: coherence describes the market reads only. A posture derived from
     zero policies cannot agree or disagree with a market reading, so it must not
     carry a rail — the rail IS the agreement encoding. It gets a different
     structure entirely (an inset strip, no rail, its own label) so the eye reads it
     as a different KIND of statement rather than a third opinion.
     §0.4: no behavioural instruction while zero policies exist — the state is
     reported, and nothing is advised. #}
  <div class="gde-policy">
    <span class="gde-policy-lbl"><span class="l-en">Capital policy</span><span class="l-zh">资金政策</span></span>
    <span class="gde-policy-state"><span class="l-en">No Grey Deer policy active</span><span class="l-zh">未启用任何 Grey Deer 政策</span></span>
    <span class="gde-policy-note">
      <span class="l-en">Nothing is restricted. This is a market read — it carries no instruction, and it is not part of the agreement above.</span>
      <span class="l-zh">当前没有任何限制。这是一项市场判读——不含任何操作指示，也不参与上方的一致性比较。</span>
    </span>
    <span class="gde-policy-count tnum">{{ _ps.get('policy_count', 0) }} <span class="l-en">active</span><span class="l-zh">项生效</span></span>
  </div>

  <div class="gde-foot">
    <span class="gde-note">
      <span class="l-en">Each read keeps its own clock, so a source that didn't settle can't vote "calm". Agreement above compares the two market reads only.</span>
      <span class="l-zh">每项判读各自计时；未结算的来源不会投出「平静」票。上方的一致性仅比较两项市场判读。</span>
    </span>
  </div>

</div>
{% endif %}
